      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "COGNAC COWBOY (2) has the hoof on the till after placing in all three runs so far this prep. Came from the back row and raced parked before finishing third at Ballarat last week. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Race fit now so gets his chance to break through. BAD GRANDMA (3) has made a solid start to her career and is yet top finish worse than fourth in three starts at Melton. Draws well again so expecting another good run. THE PRIVATE DEAL (8) is building into her campaign and is looming as a threat after a good effort from wider on this row last start, finishing third at Shepparton. Draws for a trail and should be close to peak fitness. SHESABITSALTY (9) is a three-year-old filly by Rock N Roll World on debut for Jess Tubbs. Tricky draw but has shown enough at the trials to be competitive.",
